Author: HaisenKang <haisenk@andrew.cmu.edu>
Date:   Mon Nov 2 22:32:47 2026 -0500

    Add hand fixes for scored episodes 3, 10 and 20
    
    Two opt-in env hooks in run_load_retarget.py (unset = unchanged behaviour):
    H5_MERGED_NPZ replaces the merged bundle's result.npz before cleanup, and
    H5_PATCH execs a file that redefines cleanup functions before cleaned_bundle().
    
    tools/track3/hand_fixes/ holds the per-episode fixes, tested on ken_c_scored
    with the team training recipe (3 seeds each, own-ref add_auc):
    - ep3: correct-handedness left hand (left-label HaMeR re-run of the mirrored
      left track): 0.914/0.803/0.895 (A1); A2 like-for-like 0.68 vs 0.37 baseline.
    - ep10: cup axial spin taken from the holding hand, not FoundationPose:
      spin-invariant own-ref 0.717 vs control 0.686.
    - ep20: right-hand gap refilled in the lifted pitcher's frame:
      0.730/0.904/0.881 vs 0.35-0.44.
    Scenes, rollouts and policies: HF rose-tea-cafe/v2d-t3-recon,
    experiments/haisenk/hand_fixes_v1_20261102/.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

